{
  "heading": "Checking values and method arguments",
  "notApplicable": [
    "lua"
  ],
  "axis": "language",
  "body": "Checked defines JSON rules for direct fields. Required rejects a missing or null value. NotEmpty requires a string that is not empty. The string must contain at least one Unicode scalar (one Unicode character) that is not whitespace. Its whitespace set is U+0009 to 000D, 0020, 0085, 00A0, 1680, 2000 to 200A, 2028, 2029, 202F, 205F and 3000. Length counts UTF-8 bytes for strings, elements for arrays and keys for objects. Length, Min and Max ignore a missing or null value unless a separate rule requires it. Min and Max require finite numbers, never numeric strings. Behaviors.validate(Type, value) needs no context. It checks a plain value, so the caller does not build a DTO first. Check validates its parameter before pagination, cache authorization, cache reads, HTTP or application code. Errors use validation plus a limited field.rule path, and they do not repeat the input. Unknown fields are still allowed. Tachyon does not support nested validation or validation groups. Lua has no tab here: a Lua model cannot carry `Checked` yet, so the build stops at the model file with `TY1310` (ADR 0092). Tac form validation improves the user experience (UX), but it is not the final check. Validate again in Yon. Also check authorization there, and check which fields a caller may assign.\n\nC++ has no tab here, because C++ Yon code has only route controllers so far: the build refuses `Checked` in C++ with `TY1308` (ADR 0099).",
